### Description
<!-- Please provide following data to avoid long communication and fast resolution. -->  
When I use both options together, then the `attributeGroup` gets wrapped by an extra object with the key specified by `attributesGroupName`.

### Code
```js
const parser = new  XMLParser({
    attributesGroupName: ':@',
    preserveOrder: true,
    ignoreAttributes: false,
});
const parsed = parser.parse('<root xmlns:ex="http://example.com"><p test="foo"></p></root>');
console.log(parsed);
```

### Output
```
[
  {
    root: [
      p: [],
      ':@': {
        ':@': {
          '@_test': 'foo',
        },
      },
    ],
    ':@': {
      ':@': {
        '@_xmlns:ex': 'http://example.com',
      },
    },
  },
]
```

### expected data
<!-- Please include expected output data here -->
```
[
  {
    root: [
      p: [],
      ':@': {
        '@_test': 'foo',
      },
    ],
    ':@': {
      '@_xmlns:ex': 'http://example.com',
    },
  },
]
```

